id: pm-release-ledger-origin-delivery
title: Reconcile release ledgers and tag origins with bounded publication and acceptance
description: "Connected SDK-first release-history evaluator, complete anonymous artifact-ledger reconciliation, independently verified tag-carried producer origins, unchanged-budget macOS consumer acceptance, lossless first-party publication JSON staging and eligible strict lint tooling. Implements q91, acceptance-path, ESLint and canonical artifact-weight owners plus the tag-provenance tranche of prrlce; broader display-name/manual-ordinal release work remains open. Source, hosted quality, reviewed tracker closure and actual registry/recovery evidence retain separate boundaries."
type: Changeset
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: governance,release,sdk,traceability
created_at: "2026-10-10T02:39:21.197Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T08:07:42.042Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#4d9c20054189c916e32efbab"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: Complete full-history reconciliation names all divergence classes and retains exact historical dispositions; published narrow and aggregate SDK exports compile and run in isolated Node and Bun consumers; annotated preparation and rebase retain original source identity and publication independently validates its run; full-source coverage and required quality/review gates pass; manual isolated package and CLI journeys pass without publishing.
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make release intent, delivery and origin reconstructible through reusable SDK context primitives"
value: Preserves authoritative complete release history without concealing gaps or guessing trigger origin
why_now: Canonical full census and live origin owners expose two connected remaining evidence boundaries
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Every historical release discrepancy remains reconstructible through complete SDK-backed inventories and exact reviewed dispositions; new drift is rejected, and publication preserves independently verified upstream origin across preparation and recovery."
