comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T02:39:21.197Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status census read 2914 items with zero omitted or unreadable records, plus live request search and fresh open/in-progress inventories. Prior closed Changeset pm-reliability-window-delivery delivers rolling origin/nightly series, not full artifact reconciliation or tag provenance. This record is the concrete cross-owner delivery receipt and creates no duplicate issue, reopens no completed owner, and does not close residual pm-prrlce/pm-uenmu9 acceptance."
  "2026-10-10T02:43:20.720Z","harness:codex","Manual live-provider validation caught npm12 returning a one-element array for multi-field npm view JSON, while npm11 returns one object. The current adapter refuses it; preserve this failed live receipt and add captured public metadata plus strict one-result normalization rather than weakening completeness. The shared SDK behavior and native tag/remote fixtures already pass; full verification must be repeated after this provider correction and exact source-workflow binding."
  "2026-10-10T03:22:13.348Z","harness:codex","Continuation receipt: user explicitly approved takeover of these three existing claims after normal atomic claim refused the previous session identity. Fresh strict all-status read contains2915/2915 items,2610 closed,zero omissions and zero unreadable records. Complete paginated704-issue comment census has no missing PM-file links or partial comment populations. No open PRs,Dependabot,secret-scanning or code-scanning alerts. All76 focused Node24 SDK/provider/native-Git/pipeline regressions pass. Existing code and tracker work preserved; whole-source coverage and read-only health verification are running. Live ledger control independently detects today immutable tag while publication is still in flight; no exception is added for this transient state."
  "2026-10-10T03:37:00.269Z","harness:codex","Verification checkpoint: the first canonical full-source run retained a red verdict (10,071 passed, one pre-existing MRTR input-required task test did not reach its durable state; coverage output was consequently absent). The release-focused linked command was queued behind that build lease and timed out at its existing 240-second limit; its serialized rerun passes all 76 focused tests. No threshold, timeout, denominator or ignore directive was changed. Investigating the unrelated durable-task result before accepting any full-coverage claim."
  "2026-10-10T04:04:59.922Z","harness:codex","Second canonical full-source run retained a red verdict: 10070 passed, with the ten-thousand-item aggregation and absence-tolerance default-baseline tests timing out at their existing 30000ms limits; the earlier MRTR input-required test passed. No coverage report was emitted. Final verification will use fewer worker processes to reduce contention on this host, retaining every source file, test assertion, timeout and exact integer coverage threshold. The macOS release-acceptance repair now has an independent real-provider before/after proof and a captured-output keeper regression."
  "2026-10-10T04:11:53.786Z","harness:codex","Final focused source verification passes all 118 independent SDK, collector, native tag, release-pipeline and installed-session regressions. The retained raw-init keeper failed the original source at 12247 characters and now passes without changing its 12000 ceiling. Real public control/candidate npm local, npm global and Bun sessions retain all 13 lifecycle steps under macOS-length ancestry. Branch integrated the current immutable daily release version commit through a normal merge; the final whole static and coverage gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-10T04:21:54.854Z","harness:codex","Full static verification reached the final graph-composition gate and correctly refused four newly introduced prose-only references. Added real context edges to the existing CodeFactor, MCP conformance and operator follow-up owners, and linked the completed detached cleanup fix as conformance verification history. The unchanged prose-gap ceiling is preserved; no assurance policy baseline was relaxed. Source dependency, ESLint, docstring, duplication, package boundary, grammar, token, SDK surface and cost checks all passed before that refusal. TypeScript source, strict SDK type fixtures, package and example checks pass. The complete coverage run now retains all tests and source files with four workers to reduce host contention."
  "2026-10-10T05:04:33.424Z","harness:codex","Canonical full-source verification now passes: 10074 applicable tests across 797 files, with two Windows-only tests skipped on Linux. Exact equality: statements 67756/67756, branches 51847/51847, functions 13971/13971 and lines 64469/64469. The hosted-missing-origin keeper closes the independently identified branch without changing source exclusions, ceilings, timeouts, thresholds or ignores. Mutation evidence remains 329 killed and seven explicitly reviewed equivalent cases; static verification with eligible lint tooling and hosted exact-head review follow."
  "2026-10-10T05:19:17.063Z","harness:codex","Final whole static command retained a red verdict at SDK cold-import costs: sdk 514ms versus 500, core 426 versus 423, merge 227 versus 226 and testing 486 versus 461. Earlier source, dependency, strict ESLint, documentation, duplicate, grammar, token and surface checks passed. The runtime source and SDK denominator remain identical to the earlier passing cost run; no budget will be raised. Re-run the unchanged import-cost measurement serially and retain both receipts before accepting the remaining static checks."
  "2026-10-10T05:22:32.686Z","harness:codex","Independent anonymous public baseline comparison retains the local performance limitation: published 2026.10.10 exceeds five unchanged import budgets, and this branch exceeds five in a different entrypoint set on the same busy shared host. Aggregate/core/runtime/testing measurements vary in both directions; this does not establish an intrinsic branch slowdown or certify a local pass. Both complete receipts are retained. Mandatory hosted import-cost enforcement remains required; all budgets, margins, samples, source membership and thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-10T05:23:59.402Z","harness:codex","The unchanged CLI transport-floor check also fails locally for all six fixture operations under current shared-host load (get/list/context/next/create/claim). Retain this as a second local timing limitation alongside the published-baseline import comparison, not a functional failure or a passing static result. No timing baseline or ceiling is changed. Source, schema, graph, mutation, documentation, type and security components are being completed separately; hosted CI must still enforce the complete original static command."
  "2026-10-10T05:27:39.612Z","harness:codex","All non-timing static components now pass with the eligible lint tooling: strict types, docs/skills, tracked-secret scan, graph composition, immutable history and bounded mutation enforcement. Mutation census is 336 cases: 329 killed, seven explicitly reviewed equivalent, zero unexpected survivors/timeouts/errors. Full live graph has2917 nodes14983 typed directed edges, zero missing references/active isolates/order contradictions and only the two established legacy hierarchy information classes. Validation preserves170 historical resolution warnings while history drift passes. Four implementation owners remain active for exact-head hosted quality/review verification; the broader release-origin owner is open and released."
  "2026-10-10T05:51:06.654Z","harness:codex","PR #1434 head ed33da333 completed all required hosted contexts; only Gates (static) failed on the unchanged base artifact ceiling (20,001,636 > 20,000,000), after all original import/transport budgets and bounded mutation passed. Hosted coverage and Codecov patch passed. CodeRabbit supplied one valid malformed-heading finding; failing-before/fixed-after regressions are implemented. Full review surfaces read: Sourcery quota exhausted, two Greptile expired-trial responses are availability limitations, not substantive approvals. CodeFactor Chrome PR report has no new issues (two existing repository issues retained), DeepScan exact ed33 report has zero new/fixed issues. CodSpeed reports 11 untouched CPU-simulation benchmarks and warns that createQueryFingerprint system-call time is excluded; it does not certify walltime. Fresh required Sentry/telemetry passes with zero high/critical issues, 2.73 percent finish errors and zero missing-code rows; fresh one-hour traces remain empty, so trace freshness is unverified. Five owners are now actively under verification, including reused pm-998juj for genuine artifact recurrence. Broader pm-prrlce remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-10T06:12:56.814Z","harness:codex","First review remediation is ready for a new head: mismatched changelog brackets have failing-before/passing-after controls, and lossless publication staging preserves the complete 6378-file archive with 34690 bytes saved. Both unchanged artifact profiles, native npm/Bun consumers,69 full JSON values,4731 runtime digests,strict ESLint and linked suites pass. Completed pm-998juj source work is closed and released; final hosted verification remains active here and under q91/acceptance/ESLint. All ten first-round bot comments/reviews received revision-specific reactions and acknowledgements, with the sole actionable parser thread implemented. New GH1433 remains documented/open under existing unclaimed pm-f05lsg. No new SDK publication or fresh Sentry traces are claimed."
  "2026-10-10T06:40:09.052Z","harness:codex","Greptile CLI alternative was attempted once using existing authentication after the second review push. The provider refused with code reviews are not enabled for this organization; the strict wrapper returned a red verdict, which is retained as unavailable-provider evidence, not a code finding or approval. No plan, organization setting or authentication was changed. The GitHub App remains independently retriggered on head 0f3e3da13, alongside CodeRabbit full review, and mandatory hosted checks are still pending."
  "2026-10-10T06:44:31.927Z","harness:codex","Post-push independent acceptance reinforces explicit isolation: all six narrow/aggregate SDK and complete-manifest probes pass with both PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH set to empty temporary roots for npm/Bun consumers on Node24, Node26 and Bun. An omitted manifest argument in the first supplemental launch is setup refusal and excluded from acceptance proof. Fresh backend 15-minute census has438 command_start,437 command_finish and14 command_error records, with command_finish through06:40:09UTC. Required recent Sentry/telemetry passes with zero critical/high findings,2.73 percent aggregate finish errors and zero missing-code rows; fresh traces remain unverified."
  "2026-10-10T06:46:34.016Z","harness:codex","The complete connected suite now passes as one sandboxed Node24 run:189 unique tests across seven contract files (SDK ledger semantics, public provider parsing, native tag provenance, release orchestration, installed consumer sessions, physical publication staging and artifact profiles). This replaces overlapping arithmetic with an explicit combined receipt. New heading and packing cases retain failing-before controls, while no test, source denominator, timeout or assurance threshold was removed or weakened."
  "2026-10-10T06:55:13.634Z","harness:codex","Second head0f3e3da13 passes Gates(static), including both artifact profiles and all original performance/mutation enforcement. CI coverage shard2 and macOS smoke share one failure in the existing registry-control closure fixture: required .json paths contain plain reviewed control fixture text, now correctly refused by strict packing. Repair fixture data to valid JSON without suppressing invalid/lossy refusal or changing assertions, paths, timeouts and required gates. CodeRabbit supplied the additional genuine default-branch source-run verification gap, now actively owned by prrlce. codecov/patch remains absent because full coverage did not complete; no green verdict or merge is claimed."
  "2026-10-10T07:03:13.381Z","harness:codex","All ten new or edited second-round bot artifacts were read in full, reacted to and acknowledged by revision, including the changed resolved-parser marker and inline confirmation. CodeRabbit source-branch repair has197 passing connected tests and a real GitHub/native-tag replay; broad prrlce is returned to open and released after this concrete tranche. Chrome inspection confirms CodeFactor PR has no issues and DeepScan reports zero new/fixed issues for exact0f3e3da13. Its new check links to analysis2481234; the old2481211 page still represented ed33 and was not used as new-head evidence. Final full-source coverage is running with unchanged assertions, source membership and limits; pending hosted coverage is not certified by stale Codecov data."
  "2026-10-10T07:10:05.869Z","harness:codex","Scheduling correction: supplemental PM-linked registry verification was queued while the canonical coverage runner owned the source build lease. It reached its unchanged300-second linked deadline with empty child stdout/stderr and a timeout verdict before executing assertions. Preserve the failed history/receipt and rerun the identical linked command serially after coverage exits. Direct native integration already passed all5 cases inside the197-test connected run; this scheduling failure is not erased, does not justify a longer timeout, and is not used to claim a green linked result."
  "2026-10-10T07:23:35.038Z","harness:codex","Second-review verification: the authoritative-default-branch guard and valid-JSON registry control pass all 197 connected tests, strict lint, complete types, docs/skills and docstring quality. A temporary native annotated Git tag verifies against actual repository default-branch metadata and the original GitHub run while forged or missing branch evidence is refused. The exact same PM-linked registry test now passes serially (5 tests, 28,434 ms) within its unchanged 300-second deadline after coverage releases the build lease; the earlier queued timeout remains immutable evidence. Full coverage returned 10,081 passes and one unchanged repository-scan timeout at 30 seconds, without a usable coverage report. The full 19-test absence-tolerance suite subsequently passes alone in 5.06 seconds. No source, deadline, coverage threshold or suppression is altered; the next full run reduces only local worker concurrency. Chrome confirms the exact 0f3e3 DeepScan result has zero new/fixed issues and Cubic exposes the already acknowledged default-branch thread; neither old reports nor provider availability refusals certify the next head."
  "2026-10-10T07:40:59.675Z","harness:codex","Third-round current-head evidence: c7fe7804ce27529863dda7bba1ad645ea3a41195 passes every one of the 26 effective required contexts, has no missing context and reports CLEAN merge state. This includes both previously failed macOS/coverage fixture jobs and the unchanged static/performance/artifact gates. Chrome independently reads the current c7fe780 DeepScan commit with zero new/fixed issues and CodeFactor PR with no issues; repository-level legacy analyzer debt remains with pm-z3ez. All 13 newly emitted or edited bot artifacts were fully read, reacted to and acknowledged by updating six existing relevant comments/threads, without creating duplicate confirmation replies. The parser and authoritative-branch threads are resolved, with CodeRabbit explicitly marking the latter addressed in c7fe780. The full-review request was rate-limited for 14 minutes, so its stale 0f3e3 risk summary is not new-head approval. After the stated reset elapsed, exactly one same-head full review was retriggered and is now watched natively. Greptile remains unavailable, and the separate lower-concurrency full local coverage run remains pending."
  "2026-10-10T08:07:42.042Z","harness:codex","Fourth review repair covers the real Windows release-ledger provider boundary, with failing-before vector controls and required real npm/Git native acceptance. Connected 199 tests, strict ESLint, all TypeScript projects, docstring inventory, docs/skills and workflow permissions pass; the semantic docstring debt owner pm-dvwm remains explicit. Native Linux acceptance collected 144 public versions with source-temporary cleanup and independently retained the fixture ledger disagreement. All c7 full-review artifacts have been read, reacted and acknowledged by updating existing replies. Full canonical coverage must be rerun for the changed collector; Windows CI and full current-head review are pending, without declaring old coverage or pre-review CLEAN state final."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T02:45:10.265Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence owners: the pure artifact-ledger SDK owns membership, completeness, exact-signature and stale-policy semantics; the repository collector owns anonymous provider formatting/configuration and native remote refs; the tag verifier owns native annotation/source-run binding; existing pipeline tests own preparation, early guards and rebase orchestration. These layers test different contracts rather than duplicating SDK assertions through every adapter. No coverage ignore, denominator exclusion, lowered threshold or external-API behavior mock is introduced."
  "2026-10-10T03:31:06.000Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance used an external temporary workspace with both PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH isolated. An 8,873,815-byte staged runtime distribution was installed as a real package; narrow and aggregate SDK consumers pass on Node24.21, Node26.11 and Bun, including exact settled findings, stale exceptions, new drift, incomplete inventory and caller-byte preservation. Strict typed consumers compile. Installed CLI created a custom Deployment type and Task verification child with a verifies edge, recorded comments/notes/learnings, claimed/closed/released the child and verified all eight immutable history entries plus tracker validation. An initially malformed mixed bare-id/key-value dependency argument was refused without mutation and corrected using the emitted id=<id>,kind=<kind> contract. npx --no-install and bunx --bun run the installed CLI successfully. No package was published by this manual test."
  "2026-10-10T03:58:35.135Z","harness:codex","Latest operational observation: the required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero critical/high Sentry findings and zero missing telemetry error-code rows. A fresh 24-hour Sentry trace query returned an empty complete population, so fresh tracing is not established. The telemetry backend independently reports recent command_start and command_finish events through 2026-10-10T03:43:53Z, and the local runtime reports a recent successful flush. This establishes fresh backend ingestion, not universal unsampled action capture or permanent queue emptiness. Existing CodeFactor generated-copy debt remains under pm-z3ez; MRTR full-suite timing evidence remains under pm-rs9vry."
  "2026-10-10T04:42:01.527Z","harness:codex","The four-worker canonical full-source run completed all 10073 applicable tests successfully (two Windows-only tests skipped on Linux). Exact integers retain a red coverage verdict: statements 67756/67756, functions 13971/13971 and lines 64469/64469; branches 51846/51847. The single missing branch is the hosted origin fallback in release-tag-provenance.mjs, not a product failure. Added a meaningful malformed-producer case that removes RELEASE_TRIGGER_ORIGIN from a hosted dispatch and proves it cannot silently default to operator. No denominator, threshold, timeout or ignore directive changes. Final full coverage must rerun and reach exact equality."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T03:30:23.249Z","harness:codex","Complete artifact reconciliation must preserve each discrepancy after settlement and bind exceptions to an exact missing-ledger signature. Tag-push events identify a publication request, not its upstream trigger; verify the tag-carried declaration against the original producer workflow and run attempt instead of guessing from actor or display name."
